BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-new-york-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T191348Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: New York Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's New York Fellowship puts a cross-d
 isciplinary cohort of artists\, scholars and arts professionals from Asia 
 in the United States for six months to live with a new cultural landscape:
  attending performances\, exhibitions\, workshops and discussions\, and bu
 ilding relationships with peers and with ACC's alumni network. It is delib
 erately an extended pause from daily work with NO obligation to produce or
  present anything. Applicants must be citizens or legal permanent resident
 s of an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region: Afghanistan\, Banglade
 sh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, China (Mainland)\, East Timor\, Hong Kon
 g SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Laos\, Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, 
 Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan\, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lank
 a\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. and Vietnam. ELIGIBLE DISCIPLINES (16): a
 rchitecture (design\, history and theory)\, archaeology\, art history\, ar
 ts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, crafts\, curation\, da
 nce\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studies\, music\, theat
 er and visual art\; video art and photography apply under visual art. Addi
 tional requirements: at least 21 years old by the start of the fellowship\
 , at least five years of professional experience in an eligible discipline
 \, no paid work\, university coursework or teaching (online included) duri
 ng the fellowship\, and enough confident English to handle daily life inde
 pendently\, as the J-1 visa requires. Previous New York Fellows cannot rea
 pply\, and anyone who has held an ACC grant in the last two calendar years
  is ineligible. VISA: fellows must enter the U.S. on an ACC-sponsored J-1 
 visa with no exceptions\, which bars paid work of any kind during the fell
 owship\, including work for a non-U.S. employer and participation in ticke
 ted events even unpaid. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-
 exchange and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documenta
 ry\, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running
  a concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and ful
 l-time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only t
 o travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9
 :59am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters 
 of recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novem
 ber 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funde
 d activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. App
 ly through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Ap
 plicants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee
 .\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: New York City a
 nd the wider United States. Open to citizens and legal permanent residents
  of ACC-eligible countries\, territories and regions in Asia\; U.S. citize
 ns and U.S. permanent residents are NOT eligible.\nAward: USD 38\,000 for 
 the six-month fellowship\, including a USD 3\,000 advance for travel costs
 . ACC deducts certain pre-arrival costs from the grant: the USD 220 SEVIS 
 fee\, mandatory travel health insurance (roughly USD 675 to 800) and Inter
 national House housing if you take it (roughly USD 19\,400 to 20\,600 for 
 six months). Fellows can expect USD 10\,000 to 31\,100 in hand after arriv
 al depending on insurance and housing choices. Also included: ACC-organise
 d group activities and institutional visits\, individual programmatic and 
 logistical support\, and entry to the ACC alumni network. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Six months\, in one of two cohorts: 1 January to 30 June 20
 28\, or 1 July to 31 December 2028. ACC assigns the cohort.\n\nMore: https
 ://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City and the wider United States. Open to citizens and le
 gal permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories and region
 s in Asia\; U.S. citizens and U.S. permanent residents are NOT eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T191348Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages. The Fund is r
 ecruiting one Netherlands-based designer\, maker or observer working in di
 gital culture to spend two or three months at Videotage's studio space in 
 Hong Kong in 2027\, conducting research\, broadening their network\, devel
 oping new work inspired by Hong Kong\, and presenting their findings or co
 mpleted works. The residency encourages crossovers and experimentation\, g
 iving the participant space to explore new methodologies\, widen their cre
 ative practice and produce work that pushes the boundaries of digital cult
 ure\, with a focus on social and urban dynamics. The 2027 edition takes th
 e technological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point and invites t
 he resident to respond to that theme within the context of Videotage. ELIG
 IBILITY: you are an individual designer\, maker or observer within the fie
 ld of digital culture\; you are established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, B
 onaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the N
 etherlands)\; you are registered in the business register of the Dutch Cha
 mber of Commerce (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of 
 the Netherlands\; and you have had a professional practice in the creative
  industry for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or coope
 rative ventures\, nor to designers and makers who receive a grant during t
 he work period under the Talent Development Grant Scheme\, the Open Call S
 elf-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design Practices ABCSSS. Not
 e that accepting this open call means you cannot apply to those schemes an
 d open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 5\,000 for two months or EUR 6\,500 for
  three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensati
 on for time invested and material and transport costs\; accommodation\, st
 udio use and Videotage's facilitation are covered separately by the Fund. 
 Submit your proposal to the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026
 \, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Cre
 ative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLoc
 ation: Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be
  established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint 
 Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a
  business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,0
 00 for a two-month residency or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, p
 aid by the Creative Industries Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, livin
 g expenses\, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport c
 osts. Accommodation\, use of the studio space and facilitation by Videotag
 e are covered directly by the Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Two or three months in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred p
 eriod in the application.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T191348Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Programm
 e 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:Multidisciplinary international residency at the A4 Residency A
 rt Center in Chengdu\, China\, a global exchange platform integrating crea
 tion\, networking and resources\, dedicated to fostering cross-cultural cr
 eative collisions and innovation through residency programmes while promot
 ing deep integration of creative culture with commerce and communities. Re
 sidents initiate one to two participatory local activities to facilitate c
 ommunication with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activit
 ies\, intimate sharing and exhibition opportunities to foster understandin
 g among creators and connect them with local resources. AVAILABLE DATES: S
 pring 2028 (April - June) or Autumn 2028 (July - October). ELIGIBILITY: in
 ternational applicants from any field\; A4 welcomes applications from mult
 idisciplinary artists (visual\, performing\, music\, film\, sound\, archit
 ecture)\, curators\, designers (product\, fashion\, spatial\, interactive)
 \, and interdisciplinary creatives. PROGRAMME SUPPORT: studio and accommod
 ation\; round-trip economy airfare or 2nd-class train within a set budget\
 ; RMB 10\,000 production grant per person/team (excluding living expenses)
 . DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 (2028 cycles). APPLY via the A4 Residency Art
  Center latest-recruitment page.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center 
 (A4 Art Museum)\nLocation: Chengdu\, China\nAward: Studio and accommodatio
 n provided\; round-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket withi
 n a set budget\; production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for creat
 ive production and material costs (excluding living expenses). No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: No less than 8 weeks during one of two 2028 cycles: Sp
 ring 2028 (April - June) or Autumn 2028 (July - October)\n\nMore: https://
 www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Chengdu\, China
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pier-2-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T191348Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260705
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260706
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pier-2 Art Center Artist-in-Residence Programme (PAIR) 20
 27 (Kaohsiung\, Taiwan)
DESCRIPTION:Pier-2 Artist-in-Residence Programme (PAIR) 2027 welcomes artis
 ts whose practice engages experimental approaches\, cross-disciplinary wor
 k\, and place-based research from Taiwan and abroad. Pier-2 Art Center is 
 a settlement-style arts hub in Kaohsiung\, transformed from former warehou
 se clusters\, known for diversity\, openness\, experimentation and innovat
 ion across visual arts\, music\, theatre\, cultural and creative industrie
 s\, film\, television\, and more. 2027 THEME: 'Beta Port | An Unfinished H
 arbour' - a state of becoming\; Beta Port suggests an unfixed\, in-progres
 s condition embodying openness\, fluidity and ongoing evolution\; An Unfin
 ished Harbour points to a city that continuously retains the potential to 
 be re-examined\, reconnected\, and rearticulated. PAIR approaches the resi
 dency as an open site of artistic production\, supporting artists to devel
 op works and methodologies in dialogue with Kaohsiung through research\, e
 xchange and practice. Artists are invited to take Kaohsiung as a starting 
 point and propose projects emphasising public engagement\, local sensibili
 ty\, and experimental approaches. ELIGIBILITY: open to artists and artisti
 c groups (of two people) of all nationalities with at least two years of e
 xperience in art creation. BENEFITS: studio and living space\; art exchang
 e opportunities\; round-trip economy flight or high-speed rail ticket\; da
 ily allowance of NTD 800 per person/group\; project material subsidy up to
  NTD 35\,000\; an assigned project manager. RESIDENCY 2027 PERIOD: 1 Janua
 ry - 31 December 2027 across four intervals (Jan-Mar\, Apr-Jun\, Jul-Sep\,
  Oct-Dec)\; each selected artist undertakes no less than 60 days and no mo
 re than 90 days. DEADLINE: 5 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pier-2 Art Center
 \nLocation: Kaohsiung\, Taiwan (near the Port of Kaohsiung and the Love Ri
 ver estuary)\nAward: A 33 sqm studio with private bathroom plus 16.5 sqm l
 iving space\; art exchange area and opportunities\; one round-trip economy
  class flight ticket OR one round-trip reserved-seat high-speed rail ticke
 t (depending on artist's place of residence)\; daily living allowance of N
 TD 800 per person or group\; project-based material subsidy up to NTD 35\,
 000\; an assigned project manager. No application fee.\nDuration: 60 to 90
  days within one of four 2027 intervals: January-March\, April-June\, July
 -September\, or October-December\n\nMore: https://www.pier2air.tw/en/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.pier2air.tw/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Kaohsiung\, Taiwan (near the Port of Kaohsiung and the Love River 
 estuary)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-arko-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T191348Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x ARKO Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Third edition of transmediale's residency in collaboration with
  Arts Council Korea (ARKO)\, awarded to one person of Korean nationality (
 based in Korea or elsewhere) working in digital art and moving image pract
 ices\, design\, sound and media theory. Open to artists\, researchers\, pr
 actitioners\, designers and sound artists across all formats. The two-mont
 h residency comes with an artist fee of EUR 1\,500 per month\, additional 
 production support\, and travel and accommodation support for the festival
  and residency\; duos and collectives are welcome but share the same fee. 
 Part of transmediale's 2027 programme (40th anniversary\, themed 'RFC 40')
 \, which seeks proposals offering alternatives to how we understand\, resp
 ond to and shape our technological conditions\, moving from critique to co
 nstruction outside extractive logics. Deadline: 28 August 2026\, 23:59 CES
 T.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with Arts Council Korea /
  ARKO)\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany (two-month residency around the transme
 diale festival)\; applicants must be of Korean nationality (based in Korea
  or elsewhere)\nAward: Two-month residency with an artist fee of EUR 1\,50
 0 per month\, additional production support\, plus travel and accommodatio
 n support for the festival and residency. For duos or collectives the fee 
 remains the same and is shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month r
 esidency\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/transmediale-x-arko-resi
 dency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/transmediale-x-arko-residency?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (two-month residency around the transmediale fest
 ival)\; applicants must be of Korean nationality (based in Korea or elsewh
 ere)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sam-residencies-cycle-4-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T191348Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: SAM Residencies: Cycle 4 Open Call 2027/2028 (Singapore A
 rt Museum)
DESCRIPTION:Open call for Cycle 4 of the Singapore Art Museum's residency p
 rogramme\, welcoming artists\, curators\, educators\, researchers and crea
 tive practitioners worldwide\, as individuals\, duos or collectives\, from
  all mediums and disciplines. THREE STRANDS frame the cycle\, to be interp
 reted in relation to your practice: Listening/Attuning (practices respondi
 ng critically to the urgencies of our time)\, Making/Material Cultures (ma
 terial inquiry and the process of making)\, and Beyond Human/Interdependen
 ce (relationships between humans\, technologies\, ecologies and other form
 s of life). THREE TRACKS: Artist Residency for new artistic research\, exp
 erimentation and modes of making\; Community & Education Residency for pra
 ctice at the intersection of art\, education and community engagement\; an
 d Curatorial & Research Residency for new approaches to exhibition making 
 and research methodologies. SUPPORT: shared studio or co-working space\, m
 useum resources and expertise\, network building and opportunities for pub
 lic engagement\, alongside the stipend and (for international residents) f
 lights\, housing and visa help. SELECTION: an international panel of respe
 cted voices in contemporary art. APPLY via the SAM submission portal (acco
 unt required) with a CV\, portfolio\, statement of interest of 500 to 1\,0
 00 words interpreting the thematic strands\, and a character-reference rec
 ommendation submitted by the recommender through the portal. Applications 
 1 August to 30 September 2026\, 23:59 GMT+8\; residencies run June 2027 to
  December 2028.\n\nOrganisation: Singapore Art Museum (SAM)\nLocation: Sin
 gapore. Open worldwide\; international residents get housing\, flights and
  visa assistance.\nAward: Monthly stipend of SGD 1\,500 for all residents.
  International residents (1 to 3 months) additionally receive a roundtrip 
 economy flight\, a housing arrangement and assistance with visa formalitie
 s. Singapore-based residents (up to 6 months) additionally receive a month
 ly local allowance of SGD 250. Shared studio or co-working space included.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies take place between June 2027 a
 nd December 2028: 1 to 3 months for international applicants\, up to 6 mon
 ths for Singapore-based applicants. Deadline 30 September 2026 at 23:59 GM
 T+8.\n\nMore: https://samresidencies.smapply.org/prog/cycle4/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://samresidencies.smapply.org/prog/cycle4/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Singapore. Open worldwide\; international residents get housing\, 
 flights and visa assistance.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
